Z||000005||fiero56||10-20-1999||11:14 PM||||I've got them in my Formula.  Seem to work good.  I put them in right after I bought the car.  Did one of my thourogh tune-ups.  I don't know if the car did this before or not, but when I first start it and try to drive it cold, that thing just hesitates and is pretty hard to get going.  Hesitates for a good second after every shift also(it's a stick).  I just read on the Michigan Club site about plugs, and what is "supposed" to be the best in the Fiero.  They suggest reagapping the "no gap needed" rapidfires that I have to solve this problem.  Eh, may work, may not.  I just let the car run for a minute before I drive it. I do anyway, but now I "have" to.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mshill||10-21-1999||01:27 PM||||Just put them in my 86 SE V6 when I tuned it up (just after I got it).  Don't have but 20 miles on them since I have yet to get it smogged and completely registered.||||reg||14
